    "body": "2026 SEMA Show • 2027 Dodge Charger Gets Special-Edition Package Celebrating 90 Years of Mopar\nFor Sale: Taco With Extra Topping, aka a 2022 Toyota Tacoma TRD Sport That Is Now Far From Stock DNA\n11 photos\nPhoto: Garage Kept Motors / Instagram\nThe latest Toyota Tacoma mid-size pickup truck generation arrived in North America in 2023, after the previous iteration had been on the market since 2015, bringing with it massive changes both outside and inside.\nThe fourth-generation Toyota Tacoma was announced in May 2023 with the design penned by Toyota's Calty Design Research facilities in California and Michigan and a complete switch to Toyota's TNGA-F global modular body-on-frame vehicle platform, shared with the full-size XK70 Tundra. The N400 Toyota Tacoma represented a massive step compared to the third iteration, changing the chassis, the exterior and interior design, but also the powertrains.\nSo, gone was the 3.5-liter 2GR-FKS V6 in favor of new inline-four turbo setups, complete with hybridization for the i-Force Max versions. Since its arrival, the Toyota Tacoma was extremely well received and finished 2024 and 2025 with new sales records. Even almost three years later, the third quarter of 2026 showed the Tacoma had no signs of slowing down, with deliveries up from 205k to 215k during the first nine months of the year.\nHowever, for sure, there are folks who don’t care about the N400 and still only have eyes for the classic style and technical specifications of its predecessor. For them, sitting proudly in the inventory of Grand Rapids, Michigan-based Garage Kept Motors , this 2022 Toyota Tacoma TRD Sport has a \"collection of upgrades\" to make it a capable off-road-focused machine.\nThis is a “well-equipped, adventure-ready pickup that combines the Tacoma’s legendary reputation for durability with an extensive collection of aftermarket upgrades.” It’s finished in Celestial Silver Metallic over a black interior and has exactly 60k miles on the odometer. The double cab model now has an “aggressive stance, upgraded suspension, and impressive list of equipment,” so it stands out in a crowd for anyone looking for off-road exploration, overlanding, and even some everyday driving.\nUnder the hood resides Toyota’s 3.5-liter V6 engine paired with an automatic transmission and four-wheel drive, churning out 278 hp and 265 lb-ft of torque, according to the description. The upgrades then include an OTT Overland Tailor Tuning custom computer tune and a K&N performance cold-air intake, while the suspension gets Icon 51100 upper control arms, FOX 2.5 Factory Series coilovers, FOX suspension components, additional front leveling equipment, and a ReadyLIFT 2-inch block with alignment.\nThere’s a rear differential e-locker, and outside reside things like the 17-inch Fuel Militia D725 alloy wheels, 315/70R17 BFGoodrich All-Terrain T/A KO3 tires, a 4 Wheel Parts factory-style front bumper, Smittybilt X20 Gen2 10,000-pound waterproof wireless winch with synthetic rope, and auxiliary Pro Comp and Baja Designs lighting. At the rear, there’s a Prinsu cab rack, Yakima OverHaul HD adjustable-height bed rack, Retrax PRO XR lockable tonneau cover, dual bed MOLLE panels, bed lighting, hydraulic hood lifts, and a high-lift jack.\nInside, meanwhile, there are aftermarket seat covers, an upgraded audio system featuring a Taco Tunes subwoofer enclosure, amplifier, and upgraded door and tweeter speakers. An Apple CarPlay dongle adds modern connectivity, while front and rear digital video monitoring and recording cameras are also on point for security. There’s also a rubber bed mat and other practical accessories, by the way.\nSo, how much does it cost? Well, “with its combination of Toyota reliability, four-wheel-drive capability, upgraded suspension, aggressive wheels and tires, and extensive overlanding equipment, this 2022 Tacoma TRD Sport” isn’t very cheap – the asking price is $44,900. So, what do you think – yay or nay?\nView this post on Instagram A post shared by Garage Kept Motors LLC (@garagekeptmotors)\nVia // Garage Kept Motors\nLiked the article? Follow us to see more articles from autoevolution in your Google feeds.\n2022 Toyota Tacoma TRD Sport toyota tacoma Toyota Tacoma off-road pickup truck pricing for sale Garage Kept Motors\nAbout the author: Aurel Niculescu\nAurel has aimed high all his life (literally, at 16 he was flying gliders all by himself) so in 2006 he switched careers and got hired as a writer at his favorite magazine. Since then, his work has been published both by print and online outlets, most recently right here, on autoevolution. Full profile\nUP NEXT Vancini Conversions Turns a Regular Sprinter Into a Custom, Fully-Equipped Mobile Podcast Studio",
